# Per-edge wall face lighting, measured on the REAL building north-east of the avatar.
#
# PREREQUISITE 1: a THROWAWAY clone of an explored save, --var WORLD=<name>. See
# lightmode-world.vv for the clone command and why it must be a save you can lose.
# An EXPLORED save is mandatory: terrain the character has never seen renders from map
# memory and bypasses GPU lighting entirely, so a fabricated scene cannot test this.
#
# PREREQUISITE 2: run with CBN_FORCE_SUN_HOUR=9 in the environment. The 24h sun LUT
# (sprite_batcher.cpp) sets sun_intensity to exactly 0.00 for every hour in 21:00..05:00,
# and the surface normal is consumed ONLY by the emitter loops and the sun term, so at a
# night turn this scenario measures nothing at all and still reports a clean null.
#
# Deliberately NO menu driving and NO debug views. Two earlier attempts to build a scene
# through the debug menu / Lua console ran to completion and handed back a capture while
# the terrain was never touched -- and those frames read luma 53.07 against the normal
# 57.7, i.e. a menu was still open and IN the measured pixels. Every keystroke here would
# be a way to silently measure the wrong thing, so there are none.
#
# The measurement that matters is NOT whole-frame. [facediag] counted 126 wall sprites
# against 200,000 cumulative queued sprites, so walls are well under 0.1% of the frame and
# a whole-frame delta cannot resolve them. This scenario's job is only to produce two
# deterministic, same-geometry frames; the wall bands are measured offline from the PNGs.
launch --dont-debugmsg --world ${WORLD}
waitlog "opened document .*sidebar_hud.rml" timeout=300000
focus
settle timeout=25000

# The window resizes shortly after the world loads (measured 1920x1080 then 2560x1440
# 1.5 s later), which aborts a run with "size mismatch". Discard a warm-up capture.
shot warmup avg=4
wait 6000
settle timeout=15000

# Play area only: the HUD sidebar and message bar are drawn on is_lit=false segments and
# are not part of the lighting composite, so including them dilutes every number with
# pixels this feature cannot touch.
rect play 0.25,0.12,0.55,0.80

shot faces avg=10
stats faces in=play

# A paired same-state capture is the null. Without it there is no way to tell a real
# difference between two shader builds from frame-to-frame shimmer or world drift -- and
# the world DOES drift: this save advances on exit, so clones must be re-cloned per launch.
wait 1500
shot faces_again avg=10
diff faces faces_again as=same_state in=play
assert same_state.changed < 1.0

log
stop
